TLS_Self_Signed Certificate Setup
================================================================================
The TLS_Self_Signed directory is already populated with test certificates built from:
	generate_certs.sh with the default selections.
================================================================================
If you want to build your own set of certificates you can:
run ./generate_certs.sh
	[Answer or enter all default selections at the prompts]

================================================================================


TLS_Self_Signed between jald & jal_subscribe
================================================================================

Have the following settings in jald.cfg -
private_key = "./test-input/TLS_Self_Signed/pub-certs/publisher.key";
public_cert = "./test-input/TLS_Self_Signed/pub-certs/publisher.crt";
remote_cert_dir = "./test-input/TLS_Self_Signed/pub-certs/trust_store_dir";

Have the following settings in jal_subscriber.cfg -
private_key = "./test-input/TLS_Self_Signed/sub-certs/subscriber.key";
public_cert = "./test-input/TLS_Self_Signed/sub-certs/subscriber.crt";
remote_cert = "./test-input/TLS_Self_Signed/sub-certs/trust_store_dir";

Start C Publisher (jald) with TLS -
$ ./release/bin/jald -d -c ./jald.cfg --no-daemon

Start C Subscriber (jal_subscribe) with TLS -
$ ./release/bin/jal_subscribe -d -c ./jal_subscribe.cfg

Important: If you are running both the publisher (jald) and
	subscriber (jal_subscribe) on the same host for testing, make sure
	to use a separate database for jal_subscribe (via db_root in jal_subscribe.cfg)
	to store the received JAL records.


TLS_Self_Signed (between jald & JJNL subscriber)
================================================================================
Have the following settings in jald.cfg -
private_key = "./test-input/TLS_Self_Signed/pub-certs/publisher.key";
public_cert = "./test-input/TLS_Self_Signed/pub-certs/publisher.crt";
remote_cert_dir = "./test-input/TLS_Self_Signed/pub-certs/trust_store_dir";

Have the following settings in sampleSubcriber.json -

  "ssl": {
    "Key Store Passphrase": "changeit",
    "Key Store": "<absolute path to jalop repo>/test-input/TLS_Self_Signed/sub-certs/jal_subscriber_v1_client.jks",

    "Trust Store Passphrase": "changeit",
    "Trust Store": "<absolute path to jalop repo>/test-input/TLS_Self_Signed/sub-certs/jal_subscriber_v1_client-remotes.jks",
  }

Start C Publisher (jald) with TLS -
$ ./release/bin/jald -d -c ./jald.cfg --no-daemon

Start JJNL Subscriber (jal_subscribe) with TLS -
$ cd <jjnl root dir>/jnl_test/target
$ java -jar <jnl_test*.jar> ../src/test/resources/sampleSubscriber.json
